                <pb facs="0846" n="732" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg732"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1230: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-24T18:00:00-04:00">June 24, 1931—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>45. Your 38, June 23, 2 p.m. Bolivia has formally and categorically refused to
                    consider the question of double arbitration. The Department does not consider it
                    advisable to make such a proposal as it would most surely be rejected and would
                    very likely prevent a serious discussion by Bolivia of the settlement of the
                    Chaco dispute.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
